      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway-lock): close fd when writeFile fails after acquiring lock",
        "body": "Related: #98958\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`fs.open(lockPath, 'wx')` acquired the lock but if `writeFile()` failed (disk full, quota exceeded), the code threw without closing the handle or removing the partial lock file, leaking an fd.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nInner try-catch closes the handle and removes the partial lock file before re-throwing `GatewayLockError`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible change. Prevents fd leak on disk errors during gateway lock acquisition.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Failure-injection regression test** (`gateway-lock.test.ts`) — mocks `fs.open` returning a handle whose `writeFile` rejects:\n\n```\n  it(\"closes handle and removes partial lock on writeFile failure after open\")\n  → ENOSPC injected → GatewayLockError thrown\n  → closeCalled === true\n  → lock file does not exist on disk\n```\n\n- `gateway-lock.test.ts`: **17/17 passed** ✅ (new test covers the write-failure path)\n- Sibling file-lock test already validates this same pattern: `src/plugin-sdk/file-lock.test.ts:158`",
        "branch": "fix/gateway-lock-fd-leak",
        "head_sha": "366a50c20161c558e1a54332c7bd56fd0f90cd6e",
        "author": "zhanglei99586",
